Compare RegistrationType against the enum, not against strings.

3.0.0 changed RegistrationCreationService::getRegistrationType() to return a
\Drupal\recurring_events_registration\Enum\RegistrationType instead of a string,
but three comparison sites were left comparing against the old string values. A
backed enum is never loosely equal to its own string value, so each of these
silently takes the wrong branch:

 - recurring_events_registration.module: the [eventinstance:reg_type] token
   always renders "event", even for series-scoped registration.
 - recurring_events_views.module (twice): the registrant list view always
   filters and titles by series, so instance-scoped registration lists show
   every registrant in the series rather than the ones for that instance.

Report upstream and drop this patch once fixed there.

